{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency","id":846302,"title":"2e Blood Magic: Can you keep rolling to build potency?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-12T15:30:43-08:00","id":846302,"title":"2e Blood Magic: Can you keep rolling to build potency?","content":"When using a Ritual that relies on potency (i.e. Touch of Morrigan), can you keep rolling after reaching the target number of successes so you can build more potency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T15:40:38-08:00","id":846307,"title":"","content":"I think you have it backwards. You start by &quot;building&quot; the spell and determining the Potency you want, and then roll to see if you hit the number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T15:49:32-08:00","id":846310,"title":"","content":"I think its reasonable in 2nd edition, with rituals not being something you can pull off in combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T16:06:48-08:00","id":846314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=846307#post846307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you have it backwards. You start by &amp;quot;building&amp;quot; the spell and determining the Potency you want, and then roll to see if you hit the number.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like this to be correct. Citation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T16:26:04-08:00","id":846323,"title":"","content":"Well, its how things are done in the Blood Sorcery book, with using factors. I forgot they were separate for a moment* The entire system is designed to mimic Mage's style of casting extended action magic, designed by Dave Brookshaw, and I get the impression that they're kind of designed to be used together.<br /> <br /> Officially, going strictly by only the Strix Chronicles, you can't keep rolling. You hit the Target Number of Successes, and if you happen to roll an extra success or so, those extra successes get added on to Potency. (Side bar p152, Requiem 2e core) So, if you don't use the Spell Factors, you can't keep rolling, or increase Potency in any way beyond a lucky rolls.<br /> <br /> * I consider the core book rituals unusable without Spell Factors. Or some other rulings. Honestly, I think that the mere fact the writer put the Potency rules in a side bar just goes to show how much the simplified core book rules are lacking. Such an important part of the rules put in like an afterthought! I honestly feel that the rules and rituals, as presented in the core book alone, are broken and do not work. So, take what I say with that in mind.<br /> <br /> EDIT - That said, it seems like the Secrets of the Covenant rituals don't use the Factor System; I don't see any ritual that uses Potency or needs any factors to work. I get the feeling that they're trying to &quot;fix&quot; the system by offering rituals that work with the simplified rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-12-2016, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T18:14:32-08:00","id":846359,"title":"","content":"I'm just waiting for Mage 2e to see if the new casting system can be adapted to work with Blood Sorcery the same way the 1e casting rules were. Although I have a feeling it actually won't work too well, but I at least want to give it a shot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T19:33:17-08:00","id":846392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=846359#post846359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just waiting for Mage 2e to see if the new casting system can be adapted to work with Blood Sorcery the same way the 1e casting rules were. Although I have a feeling it actually won't work too well, but I at least want to give it a shot.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think it'll work, at least not identically. Mainly because Blood Sorcery doesn't have Reaches AFAIK. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the upcoming Thousand Years Of Night will give a system for how Elders can develop advanced Blood Sorcery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T19:42:56-08:00","id":846399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=846392#post846392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't think it'll work, at least not identically. Mainly because Blood Sorcery doesn't have Reaches AFAIK.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean. It *could*. That's the beauty of homebrew. The real question will be if Reach (or a system similar to it) would even be useful for a blood sorcery system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T19:50:19-08:00","id":846403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=846399#post846399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean. It *could*. That's the beauty of homebrew. The real question will be if Reach (or a system similar to it) would even be useful for a blood sorcery system.</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't get me wrong. I'm crossing my fingers just like you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T19:53:32-08:00","id":846406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=846403#post846403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Don't get me wrong. I'm crossing my fingers just like you.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. Like I said, I get the feeling it's not going to work. But I won't know for sure until I read the full 2e spellcasting rules","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T05:19:09-07:00","id":846531,"title":"","content":"Personally, I really think we just need to back away from Mage-based rules altogether. Vampire has different concerns and issues than Mage, and nothing compared to a limit on spells on your body, or fear of paradox. I honestly think that using Mage as a basis for 2e magic rules was a mistake. YMMV.<br /> <br /> Actually, I kind of like how Werewolf does their rites in 2e. Each rite takes a different amount of time, depending on the effect, has different number of successes, specific durations and can use various dice pools depending on what you're trying to accomplish. A blood curse could take a minutes to invoke, while a larger scale effect like Apocalypse would have a long time and lots of successes to invoke. I think I'd rather be inspired by this route instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T07:10:37-07:00","id":846553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=846531#post846531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I really think we just need to back away from Mage-based rules altogether. Vampire has different concerns and issues than Mage, and nothing compared to a limit on spells on your body, or fear of paradox. I honestly think that using Mage as a basis for 2e magic rules was a mistake. YMMV.<br /> <br /> Actually, I kind of like how Werewolf does their rites in 2e. Each rite takes a different amount of time, depending on the effect, has different number of successes, specific durations and can use various dice pools depending on what you're trying to accomplish. A blood curse could take a minutes to invoke, while a larger scale effect like Apocalypse would have a long time and lots of successes to invoke. I think I'd rather be inspired by this route instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> More than anything, I loved the Symbols from Werewolf. So much, that I might consider porting them over to Vampire, with some set Symbols for Sorcery (so Cruac would always have a Symbol for Blood) and a set Symbol for Theme, with last ones being determined by what exactly the spell does...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T11:53:28-07:00","id":846659,"title":"","content":"I hadn't thought to use Rites as inspiration for Blood Sorcery, but that's pretty brilliant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T21:53:37-07:00","id":848013,"title":"","content":"I kind of hate that successes determine time and potency. It is inelegant to say the least. It should be a specific number of rolls (maybe just one, or maybe the level of the ritual) with success determining effect, or a set effect with successes determining how long it takes to succeed (I.e by having a target number needed to get the effect off.<br /> <br /> Doing it any other way us just awkward and confusing. Even if they just used both methods, but for different spells (so, some had variable potency and another took variable time to cast) it would be better. But the way it is now, the required successes might as well be the base effect, since you're unlikely to get anything more than one or two extra by accident. I don't see why you should be rewarded for managing to line up the last roll such that you only need a single success to stop (making all additional successes gravy).<br /> <br /> As to how to fix it, well, I don't know. It would basically take examining each ritual individually and adjusting it so it only has one variable (time or potency). That's definitely too much effort for me. In my last group, during 1e, there was a guy who loved the sanctum, but the current group I have all hate the sanctum and crone. They all either don't care at all about covenants or like the ordo. So, I don't really need an immediate fix, but it would be nice.<br /> <br /> As someone without werewolf 2e, how exactly can rites or symbols or whatever apply here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T01:13:33-07:00","id":848042,"title":"","content":"Werewolf rites have a predefined effect, which does not scale, a target number of successes needed to achieve it and a duration for each roll. They also have symbols, which need to be used during ritual to make it work.<br /> <br /> For example if ported to the Circle, a Cruac ritual which shows you what's going on elsewhere could have symbolbs: Blood, Eyes and something else. Then a specific ritualist, could splatter blood upon his own eyes to enact the ritual.. a different ritualist might take the eyes of a dead bird, drown them in blood, etc. (usually rites have 4 Symbols, but for ease I went with two in this example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T06:08:30-07:00","id":848108,"title":"","content":"Werewolf symbols are exceedinly good for Theban, which seems to have some very odd Sacrifices. I always had this disconnect with Theban Sorcerers carrying around a bunch of spell components like a D&amp;D wizard. Felt less like holy magic and more like ... I don't know what. But that's a whole 'nother bag of worms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T06:31:32-07:00","id":848118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848108#post848108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf symbols are exceedinly good for Theban, which seems to have some very odd Sacrifices. I always had this disconnect with Theban Sorcerers carrying around a bunch of spell components like a D&amp;D wizard. Felt less like holy magic and more like ... I don't know what. But that's a whole 'nother bag of worms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally, I'm fine with the sacrifices of Theban. Sorceror is supposed to prepare, and not carry around a bag of everything around.<br /> <br /> I loved the Symbols for a very specific reason: It makes the rituals distinct. It's not just random giberish anymore, they're different, and a player has clear tools to make it up. Not just &quot;I do some blood voodoo&quot; or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T07:08:25-07:00","id":848132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848042#post848042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf rites have a predefined effect, which does not scale, a target number of successes needed to achieve it and a duration for each roll. They also have symbols, which need to be used during ritual to make it work.<br /> <br /> For example if ported to the Circle, a Cruac ritual which shows you what's going on elsewhere could have symbolbs: Blood, Eyes and something else. Then a specific ritualist, could splatter blood upon his own eyes to enact the ritual.. a different ritualist might take the eyes of a dead bird, drown them in blood, etc. (usually rites have 4 Symbols, but for ease I went with two in this example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that sounds pretty perfect, actually. That's exactly what I said, even: only one variable, effect or time required to cast (in this case, it's time required).<br /> <br /> The symbols, well, I'm ambivalent about them. They seem like mechanically irrelevant fluff. It does seem cool, but nobody is ever going to, like, fail a ritual because of the symbols. It sounds like just forcing them to roleplay the ritual more. I'm not saying that's a bad thing--it's great--but it's not a balancing factor or anything, just a nice touch. Personally, I already felt like the rituals for blood magic were mutable. I never forced players to do it exactly like the book. But I also feel like blood magic shouldn't necessarily steal every scene as the player describes weird symbols in detail every time they cast a routine spell. Sometimes, you want &quot;I eat this bird's eyes...&quot; and sometimes you just want to move on and say, &quot;I got 5 successes this turn.&quot; It should be open.<br /> <br /> Of course, this doesn't really help reduce work--it seems like going through every ritual individually to set a potency is still required to actually copy the rite system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T07:15:00-07:00","id":848137,"title":"","content":"Oh certainly. It's a lot of work, and I'm not gonna go through it myself. I'm quite happy with the Themes system from Blood Sorcery book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T08:31:38-07:00","id":848195,"title":"","content":"Personally, I detest Themes. Its enough that I would rather not game than play in a game with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-16-2016, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T08:36:27-07:00","id":848200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848195#post848195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I detest Themes. Its enough that I would rather not game than play in a game with them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's fine too... Not gonna ask why, since this is not the topic for it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T09:59:34-07:00","id":848239,"title":"","content":"And I have no intention of going into it. But its unavoidable to talk about how the Blood Sorcery book rules do have an influence on the core book stuff.<br /> <br /> I don't like using the word &quot;broken&quot; when refering to game mechanis very often. In common gamer vernacular, its nothing more than an exaggeration for something that someone thinks is slightly more powerful than average. To me, I take the term more literally, or as close to literal as I can take it. If something is broken, it means that the something is not working properly. If I call a game mechanic broken, I mean that the game literally cannot work with the mechanics as written, and needs to be fixed in some way. Now, I made a point to say all of this so that people will take the next statement as I intend it.<br /> <br /> I fully believe that the core book Blood Sorcery rules are broken. The rituals do not work by RAW, and require either adapting the rules from Blood Sorcery (which need some tweaks from their 1e rules), or house rules. In either case, you need to make some hacks to get blood magic to work. Which is a shame. <br /> <br /> So, whenever something like this conversation comes up, I think that making up rules so the game works the way you want is something that is literally <i>required</i> to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T11:34:11-07:00","id":848295,"title":"","content":"I agree with MCN, at least to an extent. I don't think the rules for blood magic rituals are broken <i>per se</i> - in theory the system should be workable. The problem is, the rituals in the core book don't work within the 2e blood magic system. Unsurprisingly, because they were written for the 1e system, and carried over to 2e pretty much as-written. I think the rituals from the Secrets of the Covenants preview do work though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T14:30:17-07:00","id":848412,"title":"","content":"To an extent. The rituals in Secrets of the Covenant seem like they're effectively a third system (core book, core using Blasphemies and Sacraments as the first two). And I don't think that the rituals in the 2e core were meant to be 1e rituals - there's too many changes to them for me to believe it.<br /> <br /> Gaze of the Gorgon, for instance, completely bypasses the idea of Potency and altogether and moves on to a completely different way of inflicting damage. Curse of Aphrodite's Favor and Curse of the Beloved Toy bypass the core book's distance and duration issues by effectively creating magic items that store the curses. Same thing in Theban - you're bypassing the restrictions and flaws of the Requiem 2e by doing things in a roundabout way that ignores the broken parts of the rules.<br /> <br /> While I agree that the SotC rituals do work, I don't think that they're proof that the core book system isn't broken because of all the work arounds and ignoring that had to be implemented to get it working.<br /> <br /> That said, I think I might spend some time analyzing how the authors have done their rituals, and actually work on converting some of the pre-SotC rituals over to the same style of play. They do work, and they're far more simple and effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T19:42:43-07:00","id":848562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848412#post848412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't think that the rituals in the 2e core were meant to be 1e rituals - there's too many changes to them for me to believe it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're literally the exact same rituals that were in the 1e core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T20:26:36-07:00","id":848581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848562#post848562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're literally the exact same rituals that were in the 1e core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>You two are talking past each other. MCN means that the rituals were not written for 1e, they were written for 2e. Mechanically. The rules are clearly intended for 2e. You are saying the rituals are all from 1e. They are. They're those rituals, updated mechanically for 2e. The implication he is missing is that the rituals were conceived of in the first place for the 1e system, and that some are suggesting they longer work in the 2e mindset, but were shoehorned in anyway, because, legacy.<br /> <br /> Everyone is right. The point all around is that the rituals in the 2e core are lousy.<br /> <br /> I know I used to like the Circle in 1e, and I kind of hate them in 2e. For one, the corebook completely changed the flavor of them. I always liked them because they were the covenant that said, &quot;Hey, no, it's cool to be a vampire. We're natural. Just go with it.&quot; They gave purpose to your existence--you are <i>supposed to be, and it's ok.</i> The Sanctum gave you purpose and encouraged you to act in a similar fashion, but made it clear it was <i>not</i> ok. The Ordo, too, said &quot;you are totally cursed...being what you are is bad, here's how we fix that.&quot; The other two only cared about politics. So, the Crone alone said it was ok to be as you are. And I loved the Semioticions.<br /> <br /> But now, they're just, &quot;EVERYONE BLOOD ORGY JUST BECAUSE! GO PAGAN STUFF! RAWR!&quot; Much less cerebral than I liked, for sure.<br /> <br /> Then, to throw insult at injury, they ruined Cruac. You know what my favorite rituals were? Blood Witness and Cheval. Those were the ultimate spy tools--you could find out almost anything you could ever want with them. But now, you can't Cheval people on the spot...you can't catch someone down the street as they're hustling away. You can't surprise spy. You have to use it on someone willing to stand next to you for 30-90 minutes or so. What use is that? That's pointless for spying. That's just a complicated way to copy a live GoPro feed. Who cares?<br /> <br /> Reading this thread and some others I found about blood sorceries, holy crap, that's even worse! Someone described this horrifying curse they could levy on someone a mile away that infected their herd for a month with a disease that made them toxic to vampires. That's too much in the other direction--that's horrible and way too overpowered. If we have three versions of Cruac now (1e, 2e, and blood sorceries), I don't know, maybe we need a fourth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T21:40:02-07:00","id":848603,"title":"","content":"As someone who doesn't know 1e blood magic, hasn't had a chance to see the 2e blood magic rules in action, and have a player who wants to do Cruac, what issues are present in the system?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T22:07:14-07:00","id":848610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848603#post848603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who doesn't know 1e blood magic, hasn't had a chance to see the 2e blood magic rules in action, and have a player who wants to do Cruac, what issues are present in the system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, the effects of 1e rituals were created with the fact that you could enact them in seconds in mind. Yes, it might take 2 or 3 rounds, but 1 was doable and regardless, it was expected you to be able to perform the ritual within the confines of a combat, or, out of combat, within a moment or two.<br /> <br /> Therefore, most of the rituals are things that are useful in that context. Direct damage in combat, maybe, or quickly setting up the ability to see through someone's eyes as the walk by down the block.<br /> <br /> 2e, instead, requires 30 minutes instead of one turn per roll. But, they used all the 1e rituals, which, unfortunately, are things that are most useful when you only have a few seconds, rather than hours. The ability to penalize someone's next physical action is nice when it takes one turn. It's kind of pointless and disappointing when it takes an hour.<br /> <br /> So, basically, you will want to create new rituals or use some kind if homebrew from someone else or the open development stuff on this site if you don't want your pc to be mostly underwhelmed with his options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  Typo 03-17-2016, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T22:16:35-07:00","id":848611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848603#post848603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who doesn't know 1e blood magic, hasn't had a chance to see the 2e blood magic rules in action, and have a player who wants to do Cruac, what issues are present in the system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, in 1e, blood magic rituals were performed with an extended action, with each roll representing one turn of casting, and a target number equal to the level of the ritual. In 2e, blood magic rituals are still performed with an extended action, but each roll represents 30 minutes of casting, and the target number is determined by factors that are found in the Blood Sorcery book, but not reproduced in the 2e core book. Aside from the different roll intervals, the changes to how target number of successes are determined, and the 2e changes to the extended action rules, the system is basically the same between editions, which is why I maintain that the system itself is not fundamentally broken. The problem is, both edition's core books have the same sample rituals. Those rituals were originally designed to work in a system where you'd be casting them in a matter of turns. Since casting generally takes hours in 2e, most of the sample rituals are practically useless, and since the rules for determining target number of successes aren't <i>in</i> the 2e core book, it's difficult to create custom rituals to replace the sample ones if you don't have the book they are in. Then, of course, there are many people who don't like the casting system from the Blood Sorcery book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T00:51:22-07:00","id":848665,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised so many are considered useless when most seem to have a pretty good duration (though the 5 dot ones negate that benefit with taking up half the night on their own).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T02:12:48-07:00","id":848688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848581#post848581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading this thread and some others I found about blood sorceries, holy crap, that's even worse! Someone described this horrifying curse they could levy on someone a mile away that infected their herd for a month with a disease that made them toxic to vampires. That's too much in the other direction--that's horrible and way too overpowered. If we have three versions of Cruac now (1e, 2e, and blood sorceries), I don't know, maybe we need a fourth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to point out, that such a thing requires tremendous experience amounts. As far as I've seen ,most people who say the system is overpowered, have never actually tried it. Really. Even when ypou have those Themes to back it off, more often than not, you'll be constrained by time and by your own dicepool.<br /> <br /> For example, the aftermentioned ritual: He needs Destruction 2, so that's 2 base successes, You need +2 succs for One Mile Range, +4 Successes for a Month, then you need some successes depending on herd size. But let's say that the herd is 15 people, that's +4 more successes (if it's only 8 people it's +3 succs). And let's not forget that the entire Herd must be within one Mile radius of you for quite a long while. What's the chance of that? But let's say your herd is an ancestral family, and they're conveniently located in a single spot, so the One Mile range will be sufficient. Now you need Potency, how strong the poison actually is gonna be... if you leave it as is, which already is a whooping 12 successes to accomplish, it's gonna be one weak curse. Let's say we want the potency at 3 ( a medium strength ritual, I'd say), which bumps us to 14 needed successes.<br /> <br /> So now, how can we achieve 14 successes reliably? We need to roll around 42 dice(Counting 3 dice -&gt; one succ) That might turn out better.. or it might turn out much worse, because if you roll a single fail in an extended action, that pretty much gives -3 to your further rolls, and all but destroys your attempt at the ritual, unless you're much more competent than that.Oh wait, I completely forgot the resistance. So let's say the highest Composure (or Resolve) in your Herd is 3 (it could be higher, or lower, but really, we need the highest one here). So that means that on average we need 3 more dice in each roll we're making, to come out at 14 succs.<br /> <br /> So, let's say we just needed the 42 dice. That puts us at a dice pool of 7, for 3,5 hours. Without the resistance taken in. The actual stats we need is more like 9 or 10 dice pool. Which is what? 4 attribute, 4 skill and 2 at the Discipline? Or, if we put the attributes in more averages (because I found that players more often bump their Disciplines, not attributes), 3 attribute, 3 skill, 4 discipline? We're talking masters here.<br /> <br /> And this is a very superficial attempt at counting here. I'm too lazy to make maths of how good this actually is, but my gut feeling is that it's even worse, due to the Stumbled Condition which wrecks this ritual, should it come up, unless you account for it and add in 3 more dice, which pretty much means you have almost everything maxed out. Good luck, have fun with that. <br /> <br /> And after all of this - we got one fucked up herd (not even murdered or anything), for a month. And a very angry vampire on the other end.<br /> <br /> Someone with 4 of some other discipline (like Dominate, or Protean) can cause as much damage, in a more reliable way. With that many rolls, chance for one of those to come up a fail is substantially increased and that fucks up everything.<br /> <br /> However, I do agree that those rules need some tweaking, and I did get a house rule or two in (minor).<br /> And as much as I've played<br /> (My players, don't read further)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">(and even now, got two players with these disciplines (one Theban, one Cruac), they're fine. If anything, both of them are planning to buy up more normal disciplines/merits, as these Sorceries are quite hard to pull off. Cruac user is planning to get much more obfuscate first, and Theban one is buying up Majesty.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> TL;DR; Blood Sorcery book, does have a fine sorcery, it looks OP on a superficial level when people do not take account of what's possible in play. You know, theoretically a single Dominate user could rule the world by dominating everyone.. somehow that's not an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 03-17-2016, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T05:17:54-07:00","id":848717,"title":"","content":"The ritual in question was built and explained using Creation 3, Destruction 2, and Divination 2 (not that I know what these things means). He had it target the<i> vampire</i>, not the herd, and used Divination 2 to hang the effect until the vampire had fed from a certain number of members of his herd. The effect was apparently dealing 1 lethal to the vampire for each drink he took of infected blood...I don't remember exactly the details, but I know he had it down to only about 12 successes needed. The same guy in a different thread built another brutal ritual that summoned 4 aggressive bloodhounds into someone's haven when they next fell asleep for the day. That's too powerful.<br /> <br /> And I have to say, it's fairly easy to get 10 dice or so to Man+Occult+Cruac, so, I don't think even 14 successes is something I'd consider &quot;hard.&quot; <br /> <br /> Regardless, no, I don't imagine PCs would take much advantage of this system because it seems tedious/tricky to make these things work, and it might eat up the entire effective night, which reduces fun at the table. But NPCs? This kind of insane magical power would naturally wreck any setting it was introduced in as powerful Cruac masters just keep laying curses on the Prince or whatever. Still no good, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T05:29:13-07:00","id":848722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848562#post848562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're literally the exact same rituals that were in the 1e core book.</div> </div> </div> </div> They're the same rituals in the way that the core 10 Disciplines (Animalism, Auspex, etc) are the same as the 1e disciplines. If they were literally the exact same rituals, then there wouldn't be any alterations to how the rituals work. There is. Vitae lash, for instance, doesn't go up in with bonus damage, but maintains a 2L rating, and lasts for one scene, instead of a bonus equal to Theban dots and last a handful of rounds. As far as I'm aware, there isn't a single ritual without changes from 1e. <br /> <br /> Clearly, effort was put into making these work with the 2e core book system. At least on paper. The intent of the powers is roughly the same; but the mechanics that went into them are not. You exact words were &quot; they were written for the 1e system, and carried over to 2e pretty much as-written.&quot; The words are not &quot;as written&quot; in 1e. They're written different, and they were assumed to work in the game. <br /> <br /> In fact, my stance is that some of the &quot;updates&quot; to those core rituals are what broke them, and not how they were cast. Cheval, for instance, used to not require touching, and lasted for a number of nights instead of just one. I'd say that Cheval could have theoretically worked if not for those changes. If the rituals were &quot;as written&quot; I'd be much more happy with Vitae Reliquary, which now inflicts a Vinculum. As far as I'm concerned, the writer ruined that one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848581#post848581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The implication he is missing is that the rituals were conceived of in the first place for the 1e system, and that some are suggesting they longer work in the 2e mindset, but were shoehorned in anyway, because, legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm a she, not a he.<br /> <br /> And no, I'm not missing the implication. I just disagree with it. I don't think that anything was shoehorned from 1e. I feel that the writer assumed that you would be using the systems in Blood Sorcery to enhance the 2e core book rules, and designed the rituals for that in mind. I don't know if you were around when the Blood Sorcery book first came out, and I remember how the writer talked about how some of the things in that book were written with 2e changes in mind. Despite being from 1e era, I recall that there was discussion over how the rules in that book would work in 2e. There was a lot of discussion on that matter.<br /> <br /> Because of that, and the way that the 2e core rituals and magic is designed, it makes me think that the 2e system and rituals weren't meant to work as written. Its a half-system meant to be &quot;quick and dirty&quot; whereas the real rules were in Blood Sorcery. And that, in my honest opinion, is the reason why the core book system and rituals are broken - because rules to make them work right are in another book. Every ritual in the core book could work well with the Factors system in mind. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848603#post848603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who doesn't know 1e blood magic, hasn't had a chance to see the 2e blood magic rules in action, and have a player who wants to do Cruac, what issues are present in the system?</div> </div> </div> </div> Extended ritual casting, with a base time of half an hour. Very few core book rituals last longer than the night. That means that, if you want to actually do anything when you wake up, you have a very limited amount of spells you can prepare for the day. If you have one dot of Cruac, and want to prepare a single level 1 ritual, expect to spend at least an hour and half on it. Then having to shower and get dressed. By the time you're ready to go out and do anything, its practically midnight. Having more dots of Cruac and getting Exceptional Successes can cut down on the time, but that tends to exclude casual casters. Which is bad, because magic is the primary benefit of joining two of five covenants. If you want to cast a few spells AND get something done during the night? Good luck to you.<br /> <br /> Still on the issue of extended casting - rituals aren't exactly viable for spontaneous use in the middle of a scene. Lets say you have a Theban ritual that lets you determine who the liar is in a room. If you want to cast it, you need to effectively pause the scene for an hour. If there's any sort of time crunch, or even impatience, or someone unwilling to sit there while you do your magic? You're in trouble. Any interruption during this time, and the ritual fails. <br /> <br /> Some rituals are impractical to cast with the extended casting. Rigor Mortis inflicts a -3 to a physical action. Which isn't a bad effect in itself; but in practice, spending all that time to penalize the next physical action leaves you little wiggle room to choose what physical action - running around the room with a -3 penalty puts half an hour's work to waste. Cheval requires you to touch a person, meaning that your target has to sit still for the entire casting; this reduces the ritual to someone that is either completely restrained for the entire magic ritual, or someone willing. In which case, you could just as easily wire the target. <br /> <br /> Cruac and Theban have a strong tendacy to have magic that curses people. That's thematically approprite for a vampire. However, whenever you cast a spell that targets another vampire, they feel it through blood sympathy connections. And, by default, Cruac and Theban have a range of 1 mile. You can literally walk away from whomever is casting the ritual and make it out of range before they finish. Even if you pick the wrong direction, and have to walk 2 miles away from the caster by walking a full diameter of the range, the average adult can easily walk two miles within the time it takes an average ritual to complete. <br /> <br /> The base duration of the rituals tend to be either 1 scene, or 1 night. Which is a lot of effort for something that doesn't last long. Rituals in the 1e core book could have durations that lasted several nights, if not longer. Vitae Reliquary seems to be the only ritual that lasts more than a night in the core book. And that lasts one month, instead of the 1e indefinite duration. <br /> <br /> Now, none of these are really that bad when taken individually. Its the sheer weight of them all. Extended casting wouldn't be an issue if we had more month long, or even several night, abilities. But, as written, it effectively means we need to cast our rituals immediately upon sunset if we're to get any benefit. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848688#post848688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, let's say we just needed the 42 dice. That puts us at a dice pool of 7, for 3,5 hours. Without the resistance taken in. The actual stats we need is more like 9 or 10 dice pool. Which is what? 4 attribute, 4 skill and 2 at the Discipline? Or, if we put the attributes in more averages (because I found that players more often bump their Disciplines, not attributes), 3 attribute, 3 skill, 4 discipline? We're talking masters here.</div> </div> </div> </div> There are several very easy ways for you to boost your dice pool. Both the Circle and Lance have merits that directly improve their dice pools (Mandrake Garden, Library, Altar, Undead Menses). Cruac especially gets lots of bonuses. The core book includes options for additional sacrifices for more dice bonuses - merely spending more vitae or meditating (Cruac and Theban respectively) gives up to +3 dice bonus, and using elaborate sacrifices can net even more.<br /> <br /> Getting lots of dice to offset penalties is not difficult. In fact, given that we're talking about a system that's based on Mage, its kind of the assumption here. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">TL;DR; Blood Sorcery book, does have a fine sorcery, it looks OP on a superficial level when people do not take account of what's possible in play. You know, theoretically a single Dominate user could rule the world by dominating everyone.. somehow that's not an issue.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Generally, the concern isn't trying to curse a wide number of people for a month (which, when we get down to it, is actually a pretty powerful effect for a vampire; generally, that'd be a level 4-5 discipline effect). The concern is a magician spending one day a month to ritually prepare Shielding and personal enhancements that put vampires that focus on Resilience, Celerity, and Vigor to shame, invisibility that makes Obfuscate redundant, and let you be just as charming as someone using Majesty on top of all the other magical effects you have up your sleeve. <br /> <br /> The book flat out says that it is based on Mage rules, and yeah, Themes can do anything that a Mage can. And that's the problem - mages can do pretty much anything that a vampire can do with enough time and preparation. Themes might not be as good at on-the-fly effects as Disciplines, but you can ritually prepare effects that can make you a match for any Discipline. And, unlike Mage, there's no limit beyond time to the number of spells you can use to buff yourself. You can use divinations to know what threats you'll face, as well, so that also a thing. C</span>ursing people is actually one of the more difficult things in Themes. Self-buffing, protection, and divinations are actually far more effective uses of Themes.<br /> <br /> Now, it is more than possible to play with Themes in a way that doesn't overshine anyone else. But there IS a high potential for abuse in a way. And I've talked to several others who've used Themes in their Vampire game, and have recieved reports that, in those games, it was very overpowered, and was cautioned should only be used in games that include only Theban/Cruac user for PCs. So, for some games and styles of play, Theme magic is OP on more than a superficial level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T06:10:38-07:00","id":848742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848717#post848717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ritual in question was built and explained using Creation 3, Destruction 2, and Divination 2 (not that I know what these things means).</div> </div> </div> </div> Themes basically do what they say. If you want a magical ritual that either creates or summons something, then you need the Creation Theme. If you want to do something that involves hurting someone (inflict damage, reduce stats) or destroy physical objects, that requires Destruction Themes. Divination... normally, that uses magic to predict the future, read the past, etc. In this case, however? Its there strictly for &quot;trigger effects.&quot; It makes the magic hang around until the vampire performs a certain action.<br /> <br /> From the sounds of it, the ritual uses Creation 3 to &quot;summon&quot; a disease. This makes the vampire a plague carrier, and infects everyone he feeds on. Destruction 2 makes the disease toxic to vampires. And Divination to make sure it only affects the one vampire and not create a massive plague to kill everyone else off. Yeah. The spell is <i>more </i>destructive with <i>less </i>knowledge. And the worst part? This is actually just combining two examples written in the book. Its not abusing the rules, its using them literally as written on the page.<br /> <br /> For the sake of completion, there are two other Themes - Protection and Transmuation. Protection creates protections against any attempts to harm (weapons, environment, whatever) or heal. This includes protection against falling asleep. At protection 5, you can protect against banes. Transmutation pretty much covers everything else - manipulating vitae, buffing people, making people fall asleep, transforming objects into other things, and more.<br /> <br /> Like Graius said, there are practical limits that come into play in terms of preparation and time. However, if you have the time and correct Themes, there is little you can't do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T06:49:46-07:00","id":848759,"title":"","content":"Sure... But just like threads about Mages, there's one thing. People rarelly consider the XP costs or limitations. They just go &quot;This is theoretically possible, therefore this thing is overpowered.&quot;. As mentioned before hand, theoretically, a Dominate user can control an entire city, at much lower XP cost <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Really, a maxed out sorceror, will spend 80 2nd edition experience. That's 400 Beats. That's on Sorcery discipline alone, to really max out those possibilities, we either need to increase a single dicpool high and get a bunch of learned rituals, or increase 5 different dicepools (tho, I think that's a bit of a houserule on my part, as in my game, Learned Rituals use the main dicepool, while Improvised rituals use the 5 different dicepools).<br /> <br /> Really, from player perspective, this is costly from the perspective of XP alone. As for NPCs, well, those are controlled by the ST, aren't they? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, that vampire targeting Disease is even worse.. That only would have worked when the book was first released. Second edition created the sympathy link, which means that the target will know that they are being cursed, and will have time to react. Assuming some WP on their part. <br /> <br /> Anyways, the system is highly debatable, and my best advise is: to try it out. For some people it's fine, for other's it's not. I just find most naysayers have never actually tried it, and are just theorycrafting. Guess not the purpose of this thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 03-17-2016, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T08:37:33-07:00","id":848818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848759#post848759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure... But just like threads about Mages, there's one thing. People rarelly consider the XP costs or limitations. They just go &quot;This is theoretically possible, therefore this thing is overpowered.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> And then, there are those who actually have play experience and have found it to be overpowered. Play experience works both ways on the matter, Griatutis. Its not just theory crafting. Its like a crossover game involving mages and vampires. Some people find the game is a wreck with mages walking all over vampires, while others have no issues. Clearly, its something that not every game can pull off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for NPCs, well, those are controlled by the ST, aren't they? </div> </div> </div> Its not that simple. While you can restrict what NPCs actually do, there's a level of suspension of disbelief required, and a vampire sitting on all that power and refusing to use it for no good reason can cross that line for no good reason that the players can tell can make the entire thing seem kinda silly, which has a detrimental effect on the game. <br /> <br /> Some might be fine with it, and more power to them, but others will have problems with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T09:54:02-07:00","id":848848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848818#post848818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And then, there are those who actually have play experience and have found it to be overpowered. Play experience works both ways on the matter, Griatutis. Its not just theory crafting. Its like a crossover game involving mages and vampires. Some people find the game is a wreck with mages walking all over vampires, while others have no issues. Clearly, its something that not every game can pull off.<br /> <br /> Its not that simple. While you can restrict what NPCs actually do, there's a level of suspension of disbelief required, and a vampire sitting on all that power and refusing to use it for no good reason can cross that line for no good reason that the players can tell can make the entire thing seem kinda silly, which has a detrimental effect on the game.<br /> <br /> Some might be fine with it, and more power to them, but others will have problems with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I totally agree with you. And at least in my setting, vampires take precautions.. and also, my setting doesn't have anyone who's completely maxed out and can just do whatever. <br /> <br /> Anyways, let's move on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Since the takeaway from this discussion, for me at least, is &quot;try out the system, and see if it fits your needs and modify/discard it as you see fit afterwards&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:35:58-07:00","id":848866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848848#post848848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, let's move on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Since the takeaway from this discussion, for me at least, is &quot;try out the system, and see if it fits your needs and modify/discard it as you see fit afterwards&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure. So.... umm.... *looks around* What are we going to talk about? I think we pretty much answered the OP, and I don't think there's much else to talk about here. *kicks dust up*<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT - Oh, I know! So, we all agree that the rituals in the core book don't work well. And that Secrets of the Covenant rituals do seem to work well, primarily by &quot;hanging&quot; the spell through an enchanted object in many cases and bypassing the normal effects. Now, I'm interested in transforming the Theban and Cruac rituals to the same style as Secrets of the Covenant style. So, let me ask this. <br /> <br /> What rituals would people here like to see converted over to a more friendly 2e system? I know there was that thread by Rose a ways back about updating rituals, but that's been a long time, and I'm curious to hear more. Lets start a fan project about doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-17-2016, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:04:50-07:00","id":848882,"title":"","content":"Let me think... I was always a fan of the flower-power rituals in Cruac (Hawthorn Barrier, Path of Thorns and Flower of Demeter for the win). Barrier of Blood, Blood Witness / Cheval, Beloved Deodand and the divination rituals are other Cruac powers I liked. There were a few others, but I think they have equivalents in SotC preview already (or in the case of As One, is better as the new Animalism 5 power).<br /> <br /> As for Theban? Blood Lash and Haubric of Blood were favorites of mine, as was the idea of making blood-eucharist without the Vinculum. Celebricy is another power I found interesting - protect mortals against the Kiss/Assault. There were two or three bloodlines who's powers were basically upgrades to Paladin's Absolution, Purifying Light and Resistance to Disciplines. Curse of Babel, Prison of Denial, Blandishment of Sin, and Maeldiction of Despair were favorite curse-like powers. And, of course, Spear of Faith was just fun.<br /> <br /> So, what are all your favorite old rituals you'd like to see upgraded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T12:43:50-07:00","id":848925,"title":"","content":"No theban's sorcery list can be complete without one of the most iconic (at least for me) Liar's Plague :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T13:27:44-07:00","id":848951,"title":"","content":"For me, off the top of my head, Cruac was all about Blood Witness, Barrier of Blood, Cheval, Path of Thorns, Maiden's Skin, and Beloved Deodand. Thinking more about it, I saw a lot of that one that allowed quick divinations (but frankly, that can stay away), Deflection of Wooden Doom, Touch of the Morrian, the one where you took a fraction of the blood another person drank for a while, Sacrifice of Odin, the one where you became immune to blood bonds and addiction, and, quite often, NPC Amara Havana (I really had a fondness for them, for whatever reason) would use the ritual that made rain.<br /> <br /> Theban was Paladin's Absolution (though, it always felt like a cheat), Vitae Reliquary, Blood Scourge, making beetles pour out of your mouth if you lied, Hauberk of Blood, Legionaire's Blessing, Spear of Faith, um, that weird holy bird that did damage to you based on your Humanity, fucking Pharaoh's Paces!, that one where you took upgraded damage on the next attack, the zombie one (something Lazarus), and Transubstantiation (that was how I always handled communion--turn some water into blood and feed to the masses).<br /> <br /> It looks like most of that stuff was already covered, so, apparently, the same few rituals were beloved by a wide swath of the audience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T05:30:15-07:00","id":849204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=848951#post848951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thinking more about it, I saw a lot of that one that allowed quick divinations (but frankly, that can stay away)</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, that one is already reproduced in Secrets of the Covenant. Pool of Forbidden Truths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> that weird holy bird that did damage to you based on your Humanity </div> </div> </div> Bird one is also coming back, but using angels instead. Called Apparation of the Host instead. Probably because the bird one was too much like the strix now? Easy enough to reflavor if you want the birds though.<br /> <br /> I notice that you list a lot of combat stuff for Theban. Is that just because those were the ones you liked, or was it because that's how you viewed the magic, or?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T09:25:14-07:00","id":849309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846302-2e-blood-magic-can-you-keep-rolling-to-build-potency?p=849204#post849204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, that one is already reproduced in Secrets of the Covenant. Pool of Forbidden Truths.<br /> <br /> Bird one is also coming back, but using angels instead. Called Apparation of the Host instead. Probably because the bird one was too much like the strix now? Easy enough to reflavor if you want the birds though.<br /> <br /> I notice that you list a lot of combat stuff for Theban. Is that just because those were the ones you liked, or was it because that's how you viewed the magic, or?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I actually dislike Theban in general. I liked Pharaoh's Paces, but that was kind of it, and almost feel like it belongs more as a Majesty devotion anyway.<br /> <br /> I think Theban it was set up to do, basically two things: give people inconvenient, but not actually deadly or effective curses, and fight people. It feels like it has none of the utility Cruac had. Only a rare few rituals do anything actually useful outside of a fight (Vitae Reliquary, Pharaoh's Paces, Damned Radiance, and Transubstantiation stick out). And, actually, I really disliked the 1e Lancea Sanctum in general, so, you'd never catch me playing one for more than a one shot (the 2e version is WAY better to me, but I still don't care for Theban, probably because all the combat rituals are junk now with 30 minute casts and the curses are even less useful since the guy has to sit there for hours while you curse him).<br /> <br /> A guy in my group, though, <i>loved</i> the Lance and played them at every opportunity. I was just naming the rituals I remember him using a lot. I think he liked the curses about as much as I did, except for the one that made beetles pour from the guy's mouth--he liked doing that to people--and mostly just used it as a combat thing otherwise. I suspect he liked the Sanctum more than he liked Theban as well. It's just, in my mind, always been the lamer of the two vampire rituals. <br /> <br /> Like, seriously, how useful is it to give someone a Crown of Thorns? Oh, no, that guy looks weird for a while! Uh-oh! Even the beetles was more dramatic than useful. It let the guy still say nothing, unless you combined it with Dominate or Majesty or something, so, you'd just end up with silent interrogation victims. I think it was too focused on flash than substance, and relied too strongly on how the book seemed to think people and vampires would react to biblical themed curses coming true. <br /> <br /> I've always liked Cruac, though. There was a lot of utility in there, without quite as much combat focus. And the combat rituals, I felt, were mostly more useful, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}